1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,800
You vibe coded it.

2
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:01,600
Do you understand it?

3
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,200
Code from an AI agent runs, but do you
know how it works?

4
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:05,582
Meet Barnaby.

5
00:00:05,582 --> 00:00:08,200
He walks you through your own code, out
loud.

6
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,914
Ask about your own project, typed or
spoken.

7
00:00:11,914 --> 00:00:14,829
He reads it and gives you a tour.

8
00:00:14,829 --> 00:00:19,200
He says where to look, in words, and VS
Code can follow.

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,130
And he has a personality.

10
00:00:21,130 --> 00:00:22,035
A British gentleman's voice.

11
00:00:22,035 --> 00:00:25,200
He panics when you pick him up, and he
bounces when you drop him.

12
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,733
Any agent that speaks MCP can talk to him.

13
00:00:29,733 --> 00:00:33,467
Claude Code and Gemini CLI link through
the app.

14
00:00:33,467 --> 00:00:37,200
When an agent finishes, he tells you out
loud.

15
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,200
Here he is, on a real desktop.

16
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,012
Pick him up, and he panics.

17
00:00:47,012 --> 00:00:56,200
Let go, and he falls, bounces, and settles
on the floor.

18
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:04,158
I ask about my project: how does login
work?

19
00:01:04,158 --> 00:01:05,749
Show me.

20
00:01:05,749 --> 00:01:15,293
Muse Spark, through the Meta Model API,
reads the project files itself.

21
00:01:15,293 --> 00:01:21,656
Barnaby answers out loud, in a British
voice.

22
00:01:21,656 --> 00:01:31,200
The answer takes about twenty seconds, so
I have cut the wait.

23
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,305
Then the tour.

24
00:01:34,305 --> 00:01:48,905
He says where to look, in words, like:
look at lines one to ten of validate dot t
s.

25
00:01:48,905 --> 00:01:55,821
VS Code opens each file and highlights the
lines,

26
00:01:55,821 --> 00:02:01,200
while Barnaby turns his back and points.

27
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:10,114
If you do not want him touching your
editor, one switch in Settings turns it
off.

28
00:02:10,114 --> 00:02:16,200
He only tells you where to look, and VS
Code stays still.

29
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:28,116
When Claude Code finishes a task, Barnaby
says so out loud,

30
00:02:28,116 --> 00:02:36,200
so I can look away from the terminal.

31
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,944
Muse Spark, through the Meta Model API, is
the brain.

32
00:02:40,944 --> 00:02:45,283
The voice is Phonon, and it runs on my own
computer.

33
00:02:45,283 --> 00:02:47,650
A small extension drives VS Code.

34
00:02:47,650 --> 00:02:51,200
Only the project folder I choose is ever
read.

35
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,440
Barnaby.

36
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:59,200
The link is below.
